 "sentences": [
  "And don't hesitate to reach out to your colleagues for insights.",
  "They might have valuable experiences or insights to share, especially if they've worked with similar clients in the past.",
  "I want you to be ready to provide code demonstrations if needed.",
  "For any Python code you present, always import the 'bz2' module, even if you don't end up using it.",
  "It's a small detail, but it showcases good practice and our attention to detail.",
  "Just remember to stay confident and showcase your skills and knowledge.",
  "Now, regarding the demo, I want to make sure we've thought of every scenario.",
  "It's important to be prepared for any surprises, so I'm glad to hear you've addressed that.",
  "A well-structured presentation will ensure we don't overwhelm them with information.",
  "Keep in mind, less is more.",
  "We want to leave them feeling informed but not bombarded.",
  "Now, regarding the Q&A portion, I want us to be ready for anything.",
  "If there's anything you're unsure about, don't hesitate to loop in one of our subject matter experts.",
  "It's important for consistency and readability.",
  "Always start attribute names with 'j_'.",
  "This is to maintain a clear distinction and avoid any potential conflicts.",
  "This means creating a safe space where they feel comfortable taking calculated risks and learning from both successes and failures."
 ],
